College System (Person–Student–Teacher)

Problem Statement:
Create a Java program to represent a college system using hierarchical inheritance.

Create a base class Person with:

variables name and age

a constructor to initialize them

a method getDetails() that prints basic details

Create a subclass Student that extends Person:

additional variable rollNo

override getDetails() to display student details

Create another subclass Teacher that extends Person:

additional variable subject

override getDetails() to display teacher details

In the main() method:

create objects of Student and Teacher

call getDetails() for both objects

Concepts tested: hierarchical inheritance, method overriding, use of super.